So here the exoskeleton and the robot hand actually look very different from the video.

112
00:08:58,500 --> 00:09:03,720
So WAM's video pre-training helps bridge this visual gap zero-shot.

113
00:09:04,280 --> 00:09:05,520
And here comes my favorite.

114
00:09:05,900 --> 00:09:08,220
You see how natural this twisting motion is?

115
00:09:08,440 --> 00:09:11,080
You can't get that subtlety through teleop.

116
00:09:12,160 --> 00:09:15,920
Because the mechanics of DexUMI is closely matched with the hand,

117
00:09:16,190 --> 00:09:21,450
we're able to capture these fine details of human dexterity directly onto the robot.

118
00:09:23,280 --> 00:09:26,320
And then simulation is another very easy source of data.

